bsite address?","ws_tech_q6":"31. True or False: You should share your password with your best friend.","ws_tech_q7":"32. What is a 'virus' in the context of computers?","ws_tech_q8":"33. To find information online, you use a ______ engine.","ws_tech_q9":"34. An 'app' is a short name for what word?","ws_tech_q10":"35. What technology lets you talk to someone on a phone without wires?","ws_tech_q11":"36. Name one thing you can do with a smartphone.","ws_tech_q12":"37. What is artificial intelligence (AI)?","ws_tech_q13":"38. Give an example of a smart device you might find in a home.","ws_tech_q14":"39. Why is it important to be kind to people online (digital citizenship)?","ws_tech_q15":"40. What is 'coding'?","ws_tech_q16":"41. Which of these helps a computer remember things for a short time? a) RAM, b) Hard Drive, c) CPU","ws_tech_q17":"42. A _______ is used to move the cursor on a computer screen.","ws_tech_q18":"43. What technology do cars like Tesla use to drive themselves?","ws_tech_q19":"44. How does a remote control work?","ws_tech_q20":"45. Name one way technology helps us in our daily lives.","ws_tech_q21":"46. What do you call a program that can answer your questions, like Siri or Alexa?","ws_tech_q22":"47. True or False: All information on the internet is true.","ws_tech_q23":"48. What is the purpose of an 'undo' button in a program?","ws_tech_q24":"49. What kind of technology is used in a smartwatch to track your steps?","ws_tech_q25":"50. Describe one rule for staying safe online.","ws_eng_q1":"51. Which of these is a simple machine? a) Car, b) Inclined Plane, c) Refrigerator","ws_eng_q2":"52. A _______ is a simple machine used to lift heavy objects by pulling down on a rope.","ws_eng_q3":"53. What makes a bridge strong?","ws_eng_q4":"54. Name one tool an engineer might use.","ws_eng_q5":"55. If you want to cut a piece of wood, which tool is best? a) Hammer, b) Saw, c) Screwdriver","ws_eng_q6":"56. What is the first step in the design thinking process?","ws_eng_q7":"57. Why are triangles often used in building structures like bridges and towers?","ws_eng_q8":"58. A _______ is a long arm that pivots around a fulcrum.","ws_eng_q9":"59. Name a material that is good for building a waterproof roof.","ws_eng_q10":"60. What is the job of an engineer?","ws_eng_q11":"61. How does a wheel and axle make work easier?","ws_eng_q12":"62. You need to join two pieces of wood. What would you use?","ws_eng_q13":"63. True or False: Engineers only build buildings.","ws_eng_q14":"64. Think of a problem in your classroom. How could an engineer solve it?","ws_eng_q15":"65. What simple machine is found on a flagpole to raise the flag?","ws_eng_q16":"66. A _______ is a simple machine with a sharp edge, used for cutting.","ws_eng_q17":"67. Why do skyscrapers have deep foundations?","ws_eng_q18":"68. If you were designing a new backpack, what is one feature you would add to make it better?","ws_eng_q19":"69. What material would be best for making a bicycle frame: wood, steel, or rubber?","ws_eng_q20":"70. Name one example of engineering you see around you right now.","ws_eng_q21":"71. What is the purpose of a helmet?","ws_eng_q22":"72. How do gears work together?","ws_eng_q23":"73. A bottle opener is an example of what simple machine?","ws_eng_q24":"74. You want to design a boat that floats well. What shape would you make it?","ws_eng_q25":"75. What is brainstorming in the design process?","ws_math_q1":"76. What is 58 + 27?","ws_math_q2":"77. Fill in the blank: 15, 20, 25, __, 35.","ws_math_q3":"78. If a pizza has 8 slices and you eat 3, what fraction of the pizza is left?","ws_math_q4":"79. What is 9 multiplied by 7?","ws_math_q5":"80. A square has 4 sides. If one side is 5 cm long, what is the perimeter of the square?","ws_math_q6":"81. Which number is a prime number? a) 9, b) 11, c) 15","ws_math_q7":"82. Write the number 'three hundred forty-five' in numerals.","ws_math_q8":"83. What is 100 divided by 10?","ws_math_q9":"84. A triangle with three equal sides is called an _________ triangle.","ws_math_q10":"85. If you have 50 rupees and you spend 15 rupees, how much money do you have left?","ws_math_q11":"86. What is 0.5 as a fraction?","ws_math_q12":"87. Round 87 to the nearest ten.","ws_math_q13":"88. An angle that is less than 90 degrees is called an ______ angle.","ws_math_q14":"89. What is the area of a rectangle with a length of 6 cm and a width of 4 cm?","ws_math_q15":"90. If it is 9:00 AM now, what time will it be in 4 hours?","ws_math_q16":"91. Solve for x: x + 5 = 12.","ws_math_q17":"92. Look at this data set: 2, 5, 5, 8, 10. What is the 'mode' (the number that appears most often)?","ws_math_q18":"93. What is 25% of 100?","ws_math_q19":"94. A shape with 6 sides is called a _______.","ws_math_q20":"95. You buy 3 pens that cost 5 rupees each. What is the total cost?","ws_math_q21":"96. If you roll a standard six-sided die, what is the probability of rolling a 4?","ws_math_q22":"97. Which is larger: 1/2 or 1/4?","ws_math_q23":"98. Find the next number in the sequence: 1, 4, 9, 16, ___.","ws_math_q24":"99. How many minutes are in one and a half hours?","ws_math_q25":"100. If a bus travels 50 kilometers in 1 hour, how far will it travel in 3 hours?"}